WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.590
Gaima's Ambition

01:44.860 --> 01:47.230
Come back here and fight like monsters, you punks!

01:47.230 --> 01:48.390
This is such a stress relief.

01:48.390 --> 01:49.890
I'll beat your punk asses!

01:54.680 --> 01:57.460
We're definitely going to get caught if we keep running together like this!

01:57.160 --> 01:59.790
We'll have to split up if we want to survive!

01:59.790 --> 02:00.860
Their mental state has become quite like that

02:00.860 --> 02:02.360
of an impala being chased by a lion.

02:02.360 --> 02:03.680
Stay alive, Mole Crickett!

02:03.680 --> 02:05.380
Don't die, Namba!

02:05.380 --> 02:08.000
So they split up, huh?

02:08.000 --> 02:10.260
I guess they decided to wise up a little.

02:10.260 --> 02:12.060
You go that way, Blue.

02:12.060 --> 02:14.390
We'll rendezvous at the park we just passed over if we get 'em.

02:14.390 --> 02:15.530
Roger that.

02:20.140 --> 02:22.210
Oh, Vamp!

02:23.500 --> 02:25.450
Why, how are you, Mrs. Morisue?

02:25.450 --> 02:26.360
Fine, thank you.

02:26.360 --> 02:27.560
Isn't it hot out?

02:27.560 --> 02:29.640
Yes, it's really hot.

02:32.700 --> 02:36.960
I wonder if Mole Crickett and Namba are okay...

02:38.350 --> 02:39.580
Running away?

02:39.580 --> 02:40.610
Vamp!

02:40.610 --> 02:43.080
You keep sitting up straight there and wait for us, okay?

02:43.280 --> 02:46.300
I do hope nothing's happened to them.

02:47.360 --> 02:49.080
It's a dead end.

02:51.800 --> 02:54.460
Oh duh, he's a mole cricket, huh?

02:56.390 --> 02:58.610
You're underwater, I'm delirious,

02:58.610 --> 03:00.440
while she's running away.

03:04.110 --> 03:05.370
Punk bitch!

03:05.370 --> 03:08.680
Damn it, Namba!

03:09.080 --> 03:10.240
Stop it...

03:10.240 --> 03:12.150
What are you running away for?

03:12.150 --> 03:14.100
Please stop, I'm going to fall off if you don't

03:14.100 --> 03:16.320
Fine, just come down then.

03:16.320 --> 03:17.160
But...

03:17.160 --> 03:20.710
it's so intimidating when you're so aggressive like that.

03:20.710 --> 03:22.170
Please be nice.

03:22.170 --> 03:23.880
But I <i>am </i> nice.

03:23.880 --> 03:25.390
It's okay, you can come down now.

03:27.190 --> 03:30.040
Only if you promise me that you won't beat me to a pulp.

03:30.040 --> 03:31.810
You know I can't do that.

03:31.810 --> 03:34.310
That's exactly why I want you to come down from there, you know.

03:34.310 --> 03:37.010
You're not nice at all!

03:37.010 --> 03:39.150
What the hell did you just say?

03:39.150 --> 03:40.950
I'm nice, see?

03:40.950 --> 03:42.450
I'm nice!

03:41.150 --> 03:43.730
Okay, okay, you're nice!

03:52.150 --> 03:54.770
You're not going to budge from there, are you?

03:54.770 --> 03:56.440
Then I guess I have no choice.

03:58.030 --> 03:59.430
This is all in the name of justice.

04:00.230 --> 04:01.810
W-Wait a second here...

04:01.810 --> 04:04.900
Mommy!

04:11.410 --> 04:13.760
I thought I was going to die!

04:14.950 --> 04:16.090
I've been expecting you.

04:17.080 --> 04:18.810
My shoulder...

04:18.810 --> 04:21.790
I can't believe this guy.

04:21.790 --> 04:23.460
And he's supposed to be a <i>Hero </i>?

04:23.460 --> 04:24.310
Did you see that?

04:24.310 --> 04:25.130
Did you see it?

04:25.130 --> 04:28.660
That was the power of flame as harnessed by me, Weather Red the Sun Fighter!

04:28.660 --> 04:31.880
That was the power of water as harnessed by me, Weather Blue the Rain Fighter.

04:31.880 --> 04:34.370
You just used a lighter, though!

04:34.370 --> 04:36.560
All you did was use tap water!

04:39.540 --> 04:43.120
Oh yeah, I remember that happening now.

04:43.120 --> 04:45.660
Then after that we asked them for a re-match,

04:45.660 --> 04:47.260
and got really messed up.

04:47.260 --> 04:50.240
Thanks to that time, I learned to appreciate being alive.

04:52.060 --> 04:53.460
What a cruel story.

04:54.160 --> 04:56.940
And this is the picture I took after the fight.

04:56.940 --> 04:59.120
I found it when I was reorganizing the closet.

04:59.120 --> 05:02.000
Oh yeah, my tail bone was broken when we took this.

05:02.000 --> 05:03.750
I'm raising my right hand in this picture,

05:03.750 --> 05:06.800
but that's only because I couldn't move my left at the time.

05:06.800 --> 05:08.010
If Blue was still there,

05:08.010 --> 05:10.480
that means this happened while Red was still part of the Weather Three, right?

05:10.480 --> 05:12.950
Wait, weren't you around back then, Number One?

05:12.950 --> 05:15.680
Number One's predecessor was around that time.

05:15.680 --> 05:17.190
I'm actually the second generation Number One.

05:17.490 --> 05:20.090
We thought we could maybe take them two on two

05:20.090 --> 05:22.560
since Weather Yellow was taking a break back then...

05:22.560 --> 05:25.140
But damn, were they strong.

05:25.140 --> 05:27.280
That sure takes me back.

05:27.280 --> 05:30.980
Mr. Red's become so much nicer compared to back then.

05:30.980 --> 05:34.780
But why were Red and Blue so angry back then again?

05:34.780 --> 05:36.850
Oh yeah, I forget.

05:37.390 --> 05:40.330
Oh, actually...

05:48.810 --> 05:52.070
It was because I sneezed right before you guys were about to fight.

05:52.070 --> 05:55.050
Oh yeah! That's what happened!

05:55.050 --> 05:57.910
He got mad about you breaking the tension or something.

05:57.910 --> 06:01.020
I can't help it that sneezing is an involuntary mechanism.

06:01.020 --> 06:02.520
Sounds like Master Vamp, all right.

06:04.340 --> 06:05.930
Astro Fighter Sunred.

06:05.930 --> 06:08.670
This is the magnificent story of the conflict between good and evil

06:08.670 --> 06:11.140
which takes place in the city of Kawasaki.

06:15.960 --> 06:17.390
Akihabara.

06:17.390 --> 06:21.230
What was once known as the greatest electronics hub in Japan

06:21.230 --> 06:23.850
has splendidly transfigured into a new form.

06:24.850 --> 06:26.500
Sights like these,

06:26.500 --> 06:28.880
are no longer uncommon to these familiar streets.

06:28.880 --> 06:30.110
Please come visit!

06:30.710 --> 06:34.440
It's hard attracting customers lately, huh?

06:34.440 --> 06:38.290
It's like the boom's finally died down or something.

06:38.740 --> 06:41.940
I guess we won't be working here much longer now.

06:42.440 --> 06:44.210
You wanna try talking to <i>that </i> guy?

06:44.210 --> 06:45.780
He's an old man, though!

06:45.780 --> 06:48.070
But he's probably an otaku since he's cosplaying.

06:48.770 --> 06:50.260
Please come visit!

06:51.820 --> 06:53.010
A flyer?

06:56.530 --> 06:58.060
Who are you girls?

06:58.060 --> 07:01.950
We work over at a maid café called "Moe Café."

07:01.950 --> 07:04.450
Please come and rest a while, if you'd like.

07:04.450 --> 07:06.110
"Moe Café"?

07:06.110 --> 07:09.290
That is the name of a café, correct?

07:09.290 --> 07:10.190
Yes!

07:10.190 --> 07:11.550
I see.

07:11.550 --> 07:15.970
I've been negotiating with a salesman over purchasing a washing machine,

07:15.970 --> 07:17.890
so I'm pretty tired of talking right now.

07:17.890 --> 07:21.340
It may be wise to get some rest at a café.

07:21.340 --> 07:22.590
General Hengel.

07:22.590 --> 07:26.250
He is a fearless leader plotting global domination at Florsheim's West Tokyo Division

07:26.250 --> 07:28.720
with an IQ of 150!

07:28.720 --> 07:29.730
I think I will.

07:29.730 --> 07:32.050
Thank you, Master.

07:32.050 --> 07:34.370
Let us guide you to the café, Master.

07:34.770 --> 07:36.260
Master?

07:36.960 --> 07:39.570
Welcome home, Master.

07:39.780 --> 07:41.790
I leave myself to your care.

07:45.140 --> 07:48.080
What would you like to drink, Master?

07:48.080 --> 07:50.850
It's actually been bothering me from before,

07:50.850 --> 07:53.800
but are you sure you are not mistaking me for someone else?

07:53.800 --> 07:57.380
Those around me usually refer to me as "General,"

07:57.380 --> 08:00.400
but I've never once before been called "Master."

08:00.400 --> 08:03.020
Therefore, you shouldn't be calling me "Master,"

08:03.020 --> 08:04.210
but instead refer to me as you would a customer—

08:03.020 --> 08:05.490
What would you like to drink, Master?

08:09.100 --> 08:10.390
I guess I'll live with it.

08:10.390 --> 08:13.480
After all, I'm here to quench my thirst,

08:13.480 --> 08:17.750
not to correct your diction.

08:18.250 --> 08:20.780
I'll take an iced coffee, then.

08:20.780 --> 08:24.200
But then again, I guess I'm hungry as well.

08:24.200 --> 08:27.110
What is this "Omelette Rice Filled with Love" I see?

08:27.110 --> 08:30.900
It's an omelette rice made with lots of love, Master.

08:30.900 --> 08:32.720
That was a stupid question, I see.

08:32.720 --> 08:34.420
I'll take that then.

08:33.800 --> 08:35.550
As part of today's Moe Moe campaign,

08:35.550 --> 08:38.840
we're writing ketchup letters for free on top of your omelette.

08:38.840 --> 08:41.140
What would you like yours to say, Master?

08:41.140 --> 08:42.670
Ketchup letters?

08:43.440 --> 08:45.350
Then let it read "global domination"!

08:47.750 --> 08:49.800
Here you are, Master.

08:49.800 --> 08:53.310
Your Omelette Rice Filled with Love, with ketchup letter service.

08:55.030 --> 09:00.750
And so, General Hengel was able to enjoy the many different services of Moe Café.

09:03.480 --> 09:07.270
Good luck on conquering the world, Master.

09:11.260 --> 09:13.660
Looks like you've got quite a lot of tension built up.

09:13.660 --> 09:18.050
Yes, especially the arm with the scissors.

09:20.600 --> 09:25.540
I negotiated as if I would come back to buy more from them in the future,

09:21.340 --> 09:25.540
Oh really? Wow...

09:25.540 --> 09:30.420
but that salesman just wouldn't take the bait.

09:25.540 --> 09:30.420
Ah. I see.

09:33.150 --> 09:35.540
It's time for Moe Moe Scissors Paper Rock!

09:35.540 --> 09:36.810
All right!

09:36.810 --> 09:38.430
I'm going to win no matter what!

09:38.430 --> 09:40.850
Moe Moe Scissors Paper Rock is like an elimination game,

09:40.850 --> 09:44.720
and if you survive until the very end, you get to take a picture with a maid, Master.

09:44.720 --> 09:47.530
Oh no, I can't take have my picture taken.

09:47.530 --> 09:51.320
I don't take pleasure in exposing my face.

09:50.090 --> 09:51.320
Here we go!

09:51.320 --> 09:53.490
Scissors, Paper, Rock!

09:54.690 --> 09:57.940
So although their choice of words did concern me a little,

09:57.940 --> 10:00.800
it was an excellent café with a full arsenal of services.

10:02.130 --> 10:03.440
Which reminds me,

10:03.440 --> 10:06.440
I've joined the "Moe Café Club."

10:06.440 --> 10:09.280
I'll take you with me next time.

10:09.280 --> 10:11.470
Please come back, Master.

10:13.440 --> 10:15.610
We'll be awaiting your return, Master.

10:21.940 --> 10:24.200
A maid café waitress

10:24.200 --> 10:26.240
who works at "Moe Café" in Akihabara,

10:26.240 --> 10:29.890
and calls herself "Forever 17 Years Old"?

10:29.890 --> 10:31.690
Come on, now.

10:31.690 --> 10:33.090
Anyway, like,

10:33.090 --> 10:36.650
I'm worried about whether I'll be able to keep working this job anymore.

10:36.650 --> 10:37.670
Meow, meow.

10:37.670 --> 10:41.370
You should consider yourself lucky for being able to worry.

10:41.370 --> 10:44.670
Fate is very much like flipping a coin.

10:44.670 --> 10:46.820
Let's decide with this:

10:46.820 --> 10:47.640
If I win, you'll—

10:47.640 --> 10:48.590
Meow!

10:48.590 --> 10:50.340
I'd much rather do it this way.

10:50.340 --> 10:51.770
Moe Moe Scissors Paper Rock!

10:51.770 --> 10:52.710
Wait, I...

10:52.710 --> 10:54.940
Scissors, Paper, Rock!

10:54.940 --> 10:57.160
Yay, I win!

10:57.160 --> 10:58.820
I...

10:58.820 --> 11:01.530
I can only do "Rock"!

11:01.530 --> 11:04.880
Three Champagne Towers for Tomomi, compliments of Mr. Reiji.

11:04.880 --> 11:05.850
One, two:

11:05.850 --> 11:08.000
Welcome back...

11:08.000 --> 11:09.680
Master.

11:09.680 --> 11:11.140
Woof, woof.

11:20.310 --> 11:23.190
Go on, eat up.

11:26.730 --> 11:28.380
D-Don't tell me,

11:28.380 --> 11:29.850
do you not like meat?
